# BINA Sync — STAGING links (Staging-configuration builds embed this).
# UAT builds that must talk to the staging backend: build with
#   dotnet build -c Staging   (or -Configuration Staging in the scripts).
# Same shape as .env.production; see that file for key docs.
BASE_URL=https://bina-ai-staging.azurewebsites.net

# OTA update feed (version.json). Enabled 2026-07-27: it was empty because
# there was no channel separation — a staging build had no feed it could safely
# poll, since the only pointer was the fleet's. Now the STAGING backend serves
# a staging-only pointer (REVIT_RELEASE_CHANNEL=staging, prefix
# revit-copilot/releases-staging) and refuses any pointer whose channel is not
# staging, so this cannot reach a Release-channel client. Staging releases also
# publish mandatory:false — testers get a toast, never a forced restart
# mid-Revit-session.
UPDATE_FEED_URL=https://bina-ai-staging.azurewebsites.net/addin/version.json

# Web origin for the desktop OAuth browser flow (staging landing page).
LOGIN_WEB_URL=https://staging-plugins-landing-page.bypass-api-stgbinacloud.workers.dev

# Sign-in path, appended to BASE_URL → final login URL.
LOGIN_PATH=/api/auth/user/sign-in

# Optional full sign-in URL override.
LOGIN_URL=
# --- BINA Cloud (bina-be) -------------------------------------------------
# Distinct service from bina-ai (BASE_URL above) — serves /api/cloud-docs/*
# and /api/system/*.
API_BASE_URL=https://bina-be-stg.azurewebsites.net
# Web origin hosting the desktop-OAuth bridge page (/login).
CLOUD_WEB_URL=https://app-stg.bina.cloud
